&nbsp;

[^1]. :fa-lock: Adopting Orion [immediately reduces your risk](security#separation-of-concerns-and-engineering-tradeoffs10) of a major security incident. **And the peace of mind delivered matters more to your CFO and board of directors** than an [expensive ransomware insurance policy](https://thedfirreport.com/2025/02/24/confluence-exploit-leads-to-lockbit-ransomware/) you never need to file a claim against.

&nbsp;

[^2]. :fa-infinity: Setting aside the [security advantages](https://www.iconoclasts.blog/joe/wishful-thinking) and the [stiffening penalties](https://www.hipaajournal.com/what-are-the-penalties-for-hipaa-violations-7096/) for [confidentiality breaches of HIPAA data](https://cybersecuritynews.com/how-the-atlassian-confluence-breach-rewrites-data-center-security-rules/), a fundamental flaw of other wiki-like products is that they fail to provide **coherent integrations/interfaces for incorporation and periodic maintenance of externally-generated data file formats**.

&nbsp;

However, by focusing on a handful of industry standard text/source document/data formats, even your most intricate data-generated mathematical tables, graphs, charts, maps, and architectural diagrams are **fully searchable and AI translatable** in any of Orion's supported natural languages.

&nbsp;

[^3]. :fa-robot: **It's your content!** What you want is direct read-write access to it via **bidirectional version-control sync with `git`, not more opaque, pricey SaaS APIs.** Hooking your company's local Agentic AI solution into your team's wiki workflow doesn't get any safer, easier, more powerful, or less expensive than with Orion.

&nbsp;

[^4]. :fa-map-location-dot: Next, **content curation tooling** is an essential feature of Orion, not an opportunity to upsell. Our per-wiki facts database is an industry first &mdash; handy for things like managing consistent name branding or related software artifact metadata across the entire website with a 1-line edit to a [YAML file](https://github.com/SunStarSys/www.iconoclasts.blog/blob/trunk/lib/facts.yml).

&nbsp;

Instead of the inevitable, entropic link rot innate to other wiki products, you get **internal/external link validation** at page modification time during a comprehensive, pre-commit linting pass by Orion's `CMS` editor.

&nbsp;

We also provide every customer with a reporting infrastructure to **catch stale internal/external links on demand**. Even when the pages involved haven't been altered in months.

&nbsp;

Diagrams are just as easy to keep in sync with evolving alterations to the markdown prose, because with Orion's mermaid integration, **the diagram sources are embedded in the page's prose** itself.

&nbsp;

Painless recursive search / replace to repair the accumulated cruft is built into the `PCRE` search engine in the `CMS`.

&nbsp;

<span class="text-white">Measurable ROI growth across your organization is a follow-on, continuous blooming effect of the exercise of collective gardening and caretaking abilities unique to our wiki platform.</span>

&nbsp;

[^5]. :fa-scale-balanced: Furthermore, Orion scales with you as you grow, especially at the enterprise level. The <span class="text-white">**$0 per seat licensing and unlimited number of websites**</span> opens up new opportunities for controlled knowledge sharing and collaboration across teams, partners, websites.

&nbsp;

And even the entire planet with our federated platform :fa-hexagon-nodes-bolt:!

&nbsp;

We know that for most clients, just a tiny portion of those seat licenses would be used to actually edit pages, but they can use an unlimited number of "associated" read-only accounts in their wikis to share protected information with over the internet. Accounts that need not have any access to the Orion `CMS` proper &mdash; a cost-saving feature unique to Orion as the only corporation-backed **Enterprise Jamstack Wiki**.

&nbsp;

As your personnel's corporate status evolves over time, Orion makes it easy for wiki administrators to deal with the wiki reauthorizations involved. Doing a mass search and replace on every explicit `ACL` setting on the site that's tied to an ex-employee's account is as trivially automatable as onboarding a new staffer or upgrading an existing one by dropping them into the appropriate version-control authorization groups that your team designed[^ownership].

&nbsp;

[^6]. :fa-money-check-dollar: With other market solutions, [without a premium plan you are on your own](https://www.atlassian.com/software/confluence/resources/guides/premium-admin/manage-content-at-scale#what-is-content-manager). Orion's Monthly Subscription Price for a [Business Plan is ~$2600 / month for 300 seats](plans); [Confluence Premium is north of $3000+ for the same 300 seats](https://www.atlassian.com/software/confluence/pricing).

&nbsp;

As the number of seats move significantly in either direction from 300, your **savings increase**. &gt;500 puts you at our Enterprise level[^5]; and <span class="text-white">at 50 seats your monthly bill is 1/5 what you're paying to Atlassian now</span>.

&nbsp;

[^7]. :fa-arrow-right-arrow-left: Switching/Onboarding Costs from Confluence can be as low as $100 total for SMB, and amortized over the first three years of service for customers needing a more hands-on approach. The overall process is four-fold:

1. agree on desired topology of the site map from individual Confluence spaces to Orion wiki files and folders,

2. design and implement template files and build logic to accommodate above topology, branding, and desired look-and-feel of the built site pre-go-live,

3. perform an automated transform of an [`XML` dump of the entire Confluence space](https://confluence.atlassian.com/doc/export-content-to-word-pdf-html-and-xml-139475.html) into the desired source tree layout, and

4. build the Orion wiki site and return to the above steps for tweaking and retuning until customer is satisfied and ready for final contract signing.

It may appear that step 2 above is where significant costs may accrue; however the bulk of that step is amenable to AI automation. Customers may also elect to hold onto their Confluence subscriptions for as long as they like without introducing conflicts with their new Orion wikis.

&nbsp;

Finally, we tailor every installation to your specific requirements, and are **always available for consultation and professional coaching** to ensure you maximize returns on your investment in our products and services. <span class="text-white">Your team has a partner in us</span> in ensuring you see the anticipated productivity gains and customer satisfaction.

&nbsp;

### Footnotes

&nbsp;

[^ownership]. (technical) In fact, there is **no formal concept of page ownership** in the system. Orion's version control simply tracks the per-user-authorized changesets of staff at the time of the user-committed changes, lending to a more collegial corporate acculturation towards the combined work product of a wiki than in any other similar system. However, it is certainly possible to facilitate and support "ownership" moving forward with explicit `ACL` header assignments on the pages involved, and/or a custom `view` that incorporates "authorship" as an `Author` header or similar into wiki page-builds on your site.

&nbsp;

