## Leave the draining pain points of the past behind :fa-plant-wilt:

&nbsp;

For a lot of firms, Jira is a wonderfully effective tool for project management. However, over time you begin to realize that [Confluence is just tagging along for the ride](https://projectmanagers.net/top-10-cons-disadvantages-of-using-confluence/)...

If that resonates, are you tired of throwing more good money at a bad investment?

&nbsp;

Don't want to instead waste precious capital on a [nightmare to secure](https://matthiasfrank.de/en/notion-security/), [performance deteriorating](https://www.reddit.com/r/Notion/comments/1rdals6/is_notion_getting_slower_or_is_it_just_me/), [order of magnitude more expensive](https://www.notion.com/pricing), [unreliable](https://isdown.app/status/notion) SaaS service that cannot fulfill its enhanced productivity promises?

Prefer the *grokability* of a system like Orion &mdash; organized around *documents with attached data*; instead of Notion's *databases with attached documents*?

&nbsp;

Want a more conservative/sovereign/ethical approach than simply exposing all of your corporate secrets to unscrupulous AI vendors :fa-openai: and their ill-gotten frontier models?

&nbsp;

