Our global Point of Presence (POP) network :fa-hexagon-nodes-bolt: ensures low-latency connections to both Orion &trade; and the end-delivery websites we host.  We are currently on five continents :fa-hexagon-nodes-bolt: and have a bicoastal presence within the US.  And we're expanding rapidly &mdash; next up Africa and West Asia!

&nbsp;

### It's time for a sea change in how you manage and deliver your site to your target audience :fa-water:

&nbsp;

Go at your own pace, use as many employees / previews / edits / commits / branches as you like, and only pay for what you *actually use* on our infrastructure. Just bring your own AI enhanced css/javascript framework, perl scripts, and Django Templates, and we will take care of the rest of your setup at no additional charge. We recommend **Bootstrap 5** for css/js styling, as it is what we use internally; but that is entirely up to you.

&nbsp;

In addition, all clients have free, template-customizable or javascript-enabled interfaces to our powerful, proprietary `PCRE` search engine based on the Apache Licensed [`pffxg.sh`](https://github.com/joesuf4/home/blob/wsl/bin/pffxg.sh) script.

&nbsp;

<span class="text-white">Want transparency? See for yourself :fa-magnifying-glass-plus:</span>

&nbsp;

Our entire build-system logic for this very website: fewer than 100 lines of code, complete with sophisticated, memoized dependency management that auto-generates multilingual sitemaps, directory indexes, and more.

&nbsp;

View the source: [our private source lib tree](https://vcs.sunstarsys.com/repos/svn/public/cms-sites/www.sunstarsys.com/trunk/lib/), or its public [<i class="fa fa-github fa-emoji" title="Github"></i> GitHub mirror](https://github.com/SunStarSys/www/tree/trunk/lib).

&nbsp;

The underlying Static Site Generator: open-sourced on GitHub under Apache License 2.0 → @SunStarSys/orion

&nbsp;

This isn't marketing spin &mdash; it's verifiable, open engineering heritage dating back to F/OSS innovations pioneered in 2010. Ready to experience a wiki that actually saves time, money, and headaches?

&nbsp;

<center>

[Give us a call or drop us a note](/contact) today.

&nbsp;

<div class="card border-primary-emphasis fade" style="max-width:25rem;background-color:#A9BDBD;color:#392806;margin-top:10px">
<div class="card-header">Getting Started</div>
<div class="card-body">

The quickest way to get going is to play with @SunStarSys/orion's default build of <https://iconoclasts.blog> and hollow out the markdown sources in `trunk/content`.  ~90% of the styling customizations are in [`trunk/content/css/local.css`](https://github.com/SunStarSys/www.iconoclasts.blog/blob/trunk/content/css/local.css) &mdash; adjust to taste!

The other 10% involves choosing an appropriate bootstrap 5 CSS theme to replace the corresponding files in `content/css/bootstrap.*`; we recommend <https://bootswatch.com> for ideas.

The final step is to rejigger the topmatter navigation menus in `templates/main.html.*`.  Our AI translator will keep everything in sync on demand.

Need help customizing the `Perl` build system in `lib/` and other Django templates in `templates/` to fit your use case?  We are at your service!

</div>
</div>
</center>


